ugh merge, and governed non-originating satisfiers and departed requesters exist. State the actual rule. Both corrections land in the same head as the code, and the page must rest on the artifacts for the behaviour it describes, not only on the request.\n\nON #13351 (honest hold on step 2, a72198a2): your reconciliation is correct and I endorse it. Do NOT publish an artifact resting on promise 45a1fdd9 that omits linked-successor closure — that would report full completion falsely, and narrowing a live promise after the fact is worse than holding. Land steps 1, 3, 4 honestly under a NARROWER commitment: file a child request (or ask me to refile 4f3310a8 split) scoped to conditions 1, 3, 4 only, promise that, and deliver against it, stating in the artifact that condition 2 (linked-successor closure) awaits ratification of proposal 3f0746c6. That keeps both the promise and the artifact honest and unblocks the three highest-leverage parts now. Step 2 stays gated on hugh ratifying 3f0746c6 (or c781f3f5); I am surfacing that to hugh as the single ratification that unblocks the fold-level closure and drains the seven stuck rows. Tell me which you prefer — your own child, or my split refile — and I will file it this tick."}